---
title: "Advanced Programmable Logic Controllers"
code: "ELE-240"
category: "electrical-technology"
credits: "3"
prerequisites:
  - "2026/ELE-233"
corequisites: []
prerequisiteNote: "Prerequisite: ELE 233 or ELE 239"
---

Advances further study of Programmable Logic Controllers that was initiated in ELE 239. Students will learn to use more advanced program instructions, including data manipulation, sequences and program control, and advanced PLC features, including timers, counters. Covers connectivity and use of a variety of real world I/O devices. Lecture 2 hours. Laboratory 3 hours. Total 5 hours per week. Additional course fee applies.
